<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The Cyclone DDS interface for the robots run from snorlax: flatbot, and
  gen_1_5, whose cyclonedds.xml is a symlink to this file. Layered onto the
  image's fleet config by CYCLONEDDS_URI in sheppy-manifest.yaml (mounted at
  /etc/cyclonedds/robot.xml).
  Only the interface lives here; AllowMulticast spdp and ParticipantIndex none
  come from rammp-base (2.1.0-jp6 or newer).

  eno1 is snorlax's base network (the MIB, the wheels and both OAKs;
  flatbot/network.yaml).
  Left to autodetermine, Cyclone picks the arm's NIC (enp3s0) whenever it is up,
  and a node then never sees the MIB: no /base/odom and no odom -> base_link
  (measured on 2026-11-16: 0 messages, against 19 Hz with eno1 named;
  rammp-org/rammp-deployments#136). Naming eno1 alone also keeps DDS off the
  arm's network (#132). Every node runs on this host, so they still reach each
  other.

  Costs: a named interface that is down is fatal, so with eno1 down no node
  starts, the arm's included. And every node advertises eno1's address, so
  eno1 needs a stable one: a lease change on 2026-11-16 left already-running
  nodes deaf to odom.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
  <Domain id="any">
    <General>
      <Interfaces>
        <NetworkInterface name="eno1" />
      </Interfaces>
    </General>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
